{number: 136}
{title: Years I Was Caught in Sin’s Dread Snare}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Years I was caught in sin's dread snare,
Wandering [F] on in deep de-[C] spair;
Till Jesus found me in my woe,
And [G7] made me whiter than the [C] snow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Mercy there was great, and grace was free;
Pardon [F] there was multiplied to [C] me;
There my burdened soul found liberty,
At [G7] Calva-[C] ry!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
By [C] God's Word at last my sin I learned;
Then I [F] trembled at the law I'd [C] spurned,
Till my guilty soul imploring turned
To [G7] Calva-[C] ry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Now [C] I've given to Jesus everything;
Now I [F] gladly own Him as my [C] King;
Now my raptured soul can only sing
Of [G7] Calva-[C] ry!
{end_of_verse}
